    {
      "@id": "skills/process/process-core/decision-methodology-selector.md#provenance-1",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "date",
      "cat-harness:section": "2. Probabilistic / sequential decision methods",
      "prov:value": "**Two caveats on the source, measured 2026-09-30.** The monograph's abstract\npromises *\"bandit algorithms, Bayesian optimization, and tree search\nalgorithms\"*, but **v2 as ingested has no tree-search chapter** — its sections\nrun decision theory, concentration inequalities, frequentist bandits\n(explore-then-exploit, UCB), Gaussian processes, and discrete then continuous\nBayesian optimisation. And **`contextual bandit` occurs nowhere in it.** So of\nthe four rows above, two are backed by the cited source and two are not.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-30"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-30"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/process/process-core/decision-methodology-selector.md#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "date",
      "cat-harness:section": "3. Social / behavioral decision methods",
      "prov:value": "Source: Ravichandran, \"Algorithmic Approaches to Sequential Decision-Making\nand Social Epistemology\" (arXiv:2607.20636) — **for `grit-aware evaluation`\nonly.** Checked against the ingested text 2026-09-30: `grit` occurs in 35 of\nits sections; **`Delphi` occurs in none, and `nominal group` in none.** Those\ntwo come from the group-consensus literature and are UNSOURCED here; the\nattribution above covered all three rows until this was measured.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-30"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-30"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/process/process-core/decision-methodology-selector.md#provenance-3",
